COMMAND: .venv/Scripts/python.exe harness/experiments.py --help
usage: experiments.py [-h] [--params PARAMS] [--out OUT] [-n N]

Controlled mechanism, capture, priming, and prevalence experiments. All
results here are simulation experiments. Capture uses an orientation-target
analogue of Adam et al., and the unknown-color priming protocol is a model
hypothesis. Neither is labeled an exact human experiment replication.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --params PARAMS
  --out OUT
  -n N
EXIT: 0

COMMAND: .venv/Scripts/python.exe harness/study_batch.py --help
usage: study_batch.py [-h] [--root ROOT]

ACT-R confirmation of the frozen fit's secondary manipulations. These runs
have independent seeds and the shared block/practice protocol. They are kept
separate from the mirror's long uninterrupted prevalence blocks.

options:
  -h, --help   show this help message and exit
  --root ROOT
EXIT: 0

COMMAND: .venv/Scripts/python.exe harness/eye_audit.py --help
usage: eye_audit.py [-h] [--source SOURCE] [--out OUT]

Audit exported Wu/Wolfe foraging fixations without relabeling them as keypress
search. Run MATLAB's harness/export_eye_data.m first. The table comes from the
Results folder of OSF component qwm6r; RealData.csv is the separate 42/80-item
search task.

options:
